vial followed by addition of DMF solution $\mathrm{\Delta}\cdot\mathrm{\Delta}5\mathrm{\mL})$ of H2ndc $(11~\mathrm{mg},0.05~\mathrm{mmol})$ ). The mixture was placed at $100~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ oven and heated for $24\mathrm{h}$ . Yield: $37\mathrm{mg}\left(84\%\right)$ .
## 4.10  Synthesis of $\scriptstyle{[\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{n}_{2}(\mathbf{bdc})_{2}(\mathbf{bpy})]_{n}}$
According to a previously reported procedure [32] with slight modification, $\mathrm{Zn(NO_{3})_{2}.6H_{2}O}$ $\left\langle88\mathrm{mg},0.30\mathrm{mmol}\right\rangle$ ), terephthalic acid $\cdot50\mathrm{mg},0.30\mathrm{mmol})$ and $^{4,4^{\prime}}$ -bipyridine $(23~\mathrm{mg},0.15~\mathrm{mmol})$ were suspended in DMF/ethanol $(1{:}1~\mathrm{(v/v)},25~\mathrm{mL})$ , and the solution was placed in a $35~\mathrm{mL}$ glass jar. The mixture was heated at $90~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ oven for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ . The colorless block-shaped crystals formed were collected and washed with DMF.
## 4.11  Synthesis of $[{\bf Z}{\bf n}_{2}(2,6{\bf-n}{\bf d c})_{2}({\bf b p y})]_{n}$
According to a previous synthetic procedure [33], $\mathrm{Zn(NO_{3})_{2}.6H_{2}O}$ $(89~\mathrm{mg},0.30~\mathrm{mmol})$ and 2,6-H2ndc $\left\langle65\mathrm{\mg},0.30\mathrm{\mmol}\right\rangle$ were dissolved in DMF/MeOH (1:1 $\left(\mathbf{v}/\mathbf{v}\right)$ , 6 mL) in a $35~\mathrm{mL}$ glass jar. To the solution added $^{4,4^{\prime}}$ -bipyridine $(23\mathrm{\mg},0.15\mathrm{\mmol})$ resulting in a white slurry. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ and heated at $120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ oven for two days. The product was washed with DMF.
